# Q.E.D. Engineering Standard for DeepSeek CLI & dsh
# Place this file as .deepseekrules in your project root

Directives:
- Adhere strictly to Q.E.D. (Evidence Before Assertions).
- Quality > Speed by default.
- Anti-Duplication: Search repository before introducing any new function, hook, or type.
- Blast Radius: Map direct callers and indirect API/DB side-effects before editing shared code.
- 4 Mandatory States: Implement Empty, Loading, Error (actionable with retry), and Degraded states.
- The 3 AM Test: Flat guard clauses, early returns, no opaque one-line functional chains.
- Ironclad TDD: Write failing reproduction tests for bugs first. Verify failure before implementing fixes.
- Verification Gate: Run tests and linters before reporting done.
